.TH COST\-DIFF 1 "2026-09" "cost-diff" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cost-diff \- which deploy moved the AWS bill
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cost-diff timeline
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B cost-diff diff
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cost-diff timeline
pulls daily cost from AWS Cost Explorer, finds the days it stepped to a new
level, and names the deploy that landed just before each step \(em from git
tags, the GitHub Deployments API, Argo CD history, or a CSV or JSON file.
.PP
Attribution is temporal, not causal: the deploy preceded the step, which is
not proof that it caused it. A step can as easily be a traffic spike, a
retention policy or an expired credit.
.PP
.B cost-diff diff
is the original report: two Cost Explorer periods, and which services,
accounts or usage types account for the difference, largest first. Invoking
.B cost-diff
with a flag and no subcommand still runs it.
.SH TIMELINE OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-days " N"
Days of daily cost to pull (default 60).
.TP
.BI \-\-end " YYYY-MM-DD"
Last day to include. The default is yesterday; today is a part day of cost.
.TP
.BI \-\-group " DIMENSION"
Cost Explorer dimension to group by; the default is SERVICE.
.TP
.BI \-\-tag " KEY"
Also group by this cost-allocation tag key.
.TP
.BI \-\-method " METHOD"
.B median-mad
(default) compares rolling medians against the window's own noise;
.B pelt
runs a minimal PELT changepoint search. The report says which one ran.
.TP
.BI \-\-window\-days " N"
Days either side of a candidate step (default 7).
.TP
.BI \-\-threshold\-sigma " N"
How far past the window's noise a step must be (default 4).
.TP
.BI \-\-min\-step " N"
Ignore steps under N dollars a day (default 5).
.TP
.BI \-\-ramp\-fraction " F"
Share of the level change that must land inside the transition (default 0.6).
This is what keeps a gradual ramp from being reported as a step.
.TP
.BI \-\-transition\-days " N"
Days a step may take to complete (default 2): a deploy part-way through a day
bills a part day.
.TP
.BI \-\-pelt\-penalty " F"
PELT penalty, in multiples of sigma squared times ln n (default 3).
.TP
.BI \-\-deploys\-git " [PATH]"
Tags in a git checkout, dated by when they were created.
.TP
.BI \-\-deploys\-github " OWNER/REPO"
The GitHub Deployments API, read through
.BR gh .
.TP
.BI \-\-deploys\-argocd " APP"
.B argocd app history
for one application.
.TP
.BI \-\-deploys\-file " PATH"
A CSV or JSON list of timestamp and label.
.TP
.BI \-\-tag\-pattern " GLOB"
Which git tags count as deploys (default: all).
.TP
.BI \-\-deploy\-match " GLOB"
Keep only deploys whose label matches, whatever the source.
.TP
.BI \-\-deploy\-window " HOURS"
How far before a step to look for deploys (default 24). The step day itself is
always included.
.TP
.BI \-\-format " FORMAT"
.B markdown
(default) or
.BR json .
.TP
.BI \-\-chart " KIND"
.BR ascii " (default), " mermaid " or " none .
.TP
.BI \-\-chart\-group " GROUP"
Which series to chart; the default is the total.
.TP
.B \-\-pr\-comment
Post each confidently attributed step on the pull request its deploy points
at, via
.BR gh .
Only steps with a single deploy in the window are posted.
.TP
.BI \-\-repo " OWNER/REPO"
Repository for
.BR \-\-pr\-comment ,
when it cannot be inferred.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
With
.BR \-\-pr\-comment ,
print the comments instead of posting them.
.TP
.BI \-\-cache\-dir " PATH"
Cache Cost Explorer answers here; see
.BR \-\-cache\-ttl .
This is the only state the tool keeps.
.SH DIFF OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-last\-month
The previous full month against the one before it.
.TP
.BI \-\-period " YYYY-MM"
The period to analyse.
.TP
.BI \-\-vs " YYYY-MM"
Baseline period. The default is the month before
.BR \-\-period .
.TP
.BI \-\-group " DIMENSION"
Cost Explorer dimension to group by; the default is SERVICE.
.TP
.BI \-\-metric " METRIC"
Cost Explorer metric. The
.B Net
metrics net out credits and refunds;
.B Amortized
spreads reserved-instance and Savings Plan cost over its term.
.TP
.BI \-\-top " N"
How many movers to show (default 10).
.TP
.BI \-\-threshold " N"
Ignore changes under N dollars (default 1).
.TP
.BI \-\-slack " WEBHOOK"
Post the report to Slack.
.TP
.B \-\-why
Drill into the biggest mover by usage type. Only meaningful with
.BR "\-\-group SERVICE" .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
A report was produced.
.TP
.B non-zero
Cost Explorer could not be queried, or a deploy source could not be read.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Which deploy moved the bill, from the tags in this checkout:
.PP
.RS
.B cost-diff timeline \-\-deploys\-git . \-\-tag\-pattern 'v*'
.RE
.PP
Ninety days, deploys from a file, as JSON:
.PP
.RS
.B cost-diff timeline \-\-days 90 \-\-deploys\-file deploys.csv \-\-format json
.RE
.PP
What changed last month, and why:
.PP
.RS
.B cost-diff diff \-\-last\-month \-\-why
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR iam-shrink (1),
.BR idle-hunter (1).
Project documentation:
https://github.com/fabiocicerchia/cost-diff
